# Ghostly Keybearer's target is a Room "you control": Bot2's Unholy Annex (cast on turn 2 with three Moxen) is refused on turn 3, when the Keybearer first hits
# Bot2 (positive control: Bot1's own Annex is taken and its right door is unlocked, making the Demon). On turn 5 the hit targets that Room again, now fully unlocked:
# it is still a legal target (CR 115.1) with no locked door, so nothing is unlocked and no second Demon is made. The Keybearer's own flight keeps Bot2
# without a blocker both turns. Bot2 loses life to the Annexes it draws with: 2 at its own end step (no Demon of its own), and 2 at Bot1's end step once the Demon is out (18 -> 15 after the first hit; 13 -> 11 -> 8 after the second).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Ghostly Keybearer
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber
Island x16

